snake/ is ported from mizorewww/laya-mlx (Apache-2.0, see LICENSE-laya-mlx).

Modifications against the upstream laya_mlx/snake module:
- shim.py (new): maps laya_mlx.Agent's predict(state, questions) onto the
  system1-omni /v1/systemone request/response contract.
- snake/policy.py: decision backend swapped to shim.SystemOneBackend; metadata
  records backend health/URL instead of a local MLX checkpoint. decide() is
  verbatim upstream.
- snake/cli.py: --backend/--model replace the local-checkpoint arguments;
  --optimize and the benchmark subcommand dropped (no-op against a remote
  backend / not re-validated); startup message and summary "network" field
  follow the backend.
- snake/ui.py: title/engine/network rows read backend-driven stats instead of
  the upstream hard-coded MLX strings.
- snake/replay.py: ffmpeg command assembly factored into ffmpeg_mp4_cmd for
  reuse by multi_replay; raster sizing includes line spacing to keep tall
  grids inside the output image. Raster fonts resolve
  per-platform (macOS Menlo, Linux DejaVu Sans Mono, Windows Consola), or
  via --font.
- snake/warmup.py (new): warmup shared by cli.py and multi.py; stops before
  deciding again on a won or dead game (the upstream inline warmup in cli.py
  only checked dead).
- snake/multi.py, snake/multi_ui.py, snake/multi_replay.py (new): N-game
  orchestration, grid composition and replay rendering. Stop sibling games
  on failure or interruption, sort concurrent frames by timestamp and size
  grid slots from the board dimensions.
- Formatting: all Python files were reformatted to the repository ruff style
  (ruff format); snake/{game,__init__,__main__}.py carry no functional changes.
